{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>You have seen.</b> It is no tradition handed to you, not in words do I send to you, not by witnesses do I testify for you — but <b>you have seen what I did to Egypt</b>: how many transgressions they owed Me before you were joined to you, yet I did not exact payment from them except through you (Mekhilta)." "<b>And I bore you.</b> This is the day Israel came to Rameses — for Israel were scattered throughout all the land of Goshen, and in a brief moment, when they came to journey and depart, they all gathered to Rameses. And Onkelos rendered וָאֶשָּׂא like וָאַסִּיעַ אֶתְכֶם — 'וְאַטֵּלִית יָתְכוֹן'; he adjusted the matter in a manner of honor from on high." "<b>On eagles' wings.</b> Like the eagle that carries its fledglings on its wings — for all other birds place their young between their feet, because they fear another bird flying above them. But this eagle fears only man — lest he shoot an arrow at it — since no bird flies above it; therefore it places its young on its wings. It says: rather let the arrow enter me and not my child. So too did I: ״וַיִּסַּע מַלְאַךְ הָאֱלֹהִים וגו׳, וַיָּבֹא בֵּין מַחֲנֵה מִצְרַיִם וגו׳״ (Exodus 14) — and the Egyptians were shooting arrows and catapult-stones, and the cloud received them." "<b>And I brought you to Me.</b> As its Targum renders."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:07.897216068Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}